 "flaws": [
  "<b>Same open gates as v8.</b> Shoulder abduction at contact is 151° (target 100–125), the trunk arch at the racket low point is 32° (target 40–50; v8 30°), and the kinetic chain fails only on the knee → pelvis lag (133 ms; v8 125 ms), which comes from the jump timing. These are unchanged v8 items.",
  "<b>Racket speed 41.7 m/s</b> passes (< 50), but it is above real kick serves (30–40 m/s; v8 25.6). The faster, later racket drop shortens the upswing.",
  "<b>Racket–body clearance 70 mm</b> (v8 139 mm), because the follow-through racket now passes lower, beside the left leg.",
  "<b>The arm timing comes from one side-on clip</b> (pro, slow motion, real speed from the ball toss), sampled as 7 authored joint-angle keys and smoothed. The follow-through keys are set by hand from the same clip; the clip's post-contact arm angles are too noisy to copy directly."
